Relevant columns and how they will be used  
• pizza_clean_customer_orders.order_id : main key that identifies every customer order  
• pizza_clean_customer_orders.pizza_id : tells us which pizza was bought so we can attach the right price ($12 or $10)  
• pizza_get_extras.order_id      : lets us find the same order in the extras table  
• pizza_get_extras.extras_count    : number of extra toppings (each charged $1) for that order  
• pizza_clean_runner_orders.order_id  : joins the runner‑delivery information to the order  
• pizza_clean_runner_orders.cancellation : if NULL the order was delivered (needed filter)  
• pizza_names.pizza_id / pizza_names.pizza_name : reference list of pizzas (helps check that id 1 = Meat Lovers, id 2 = Vegetarian)  

Key conditions  
1. Only keep rows where pizza_clean_runner_orders.cancellation IS NULL  
2. Only pizzas 1 and 2 matter (Meat Lovers and Vegetarian)  
3. Each Meat Lovers pizza contributes $12 and each Vegetarian contributes $10  
4. Every extra topping (sum of extras_count for an order) adds $1  

Below are ten exploratory queries (from simple look‑ups to the final revenue query).  
Every query is limited to 20 rows so they are always “safe” to run while investigating.

```sql
-- 1. All pizzas and their names
SELECT DISTINCT pn.pizza_id, pn.pizza_name
FROM pizza_names AS pn
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Raw list of customer orders
SELECT DISTINCT order_id, customer_id, pizza_id, extras
FROM pizza_clean_customer_orders
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Only Meat Lovers & Vegetarian orders (by id)
SELECT order_id, pizza_id
FROM pizza_clean_customer_orders
WHERE pizza_id IN (1, 2)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Check delivery status for those orders
SELECT cco.order_id, cro.cancellation
FROM pizza_clean_customer_orders AS cco
JOIN pizza_clean_runner_orders AS cro
  ON cco.order_id = cro.order_id
WHERE cco.pizza_id IN (1, 2)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Extras recorded for any order
SELECT DISTINCT order_id, extras, extras_count
FROM pizza_get_extras
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Total number of extras per order
SELECT order_id, SUM(extras_count) AS total_extras
FROM pizza_get_extras
GROUP BY order_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Orders, prices (no extras yet), and delivered flag
SELECT cco.order_id,
       CASE WHEN cco.pizza_id = 1 THEN 12 ELSE 10 END AS base_price,
       cro.cancellation
FROM pizza_clean_customer_orders AS cco
JOIN pizza_clean_runner_orders  AS cro USING (order_id)
WHERE cco.pizza_id IN (1, 2)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Orders with extras and delivered flag
SELECT cco.order_id,
       CASE WHEN cco.pizza_id = 1 THEN 12 ELSE 10 END AS base_price,
       COALESCE(ge.total_extras, 0)                  AS extras_qty,
       cro.cancellation
FROM pizza_clean_customer_orders AS cco
JOIN pizza_clean_runner_orders  AS cro USING (order_id)
LEFT JOIN (
     SELECT order_id, SUM(extras_count) AS total_extras
     FROM   pizza_get_extras
     GROUP BY order_id
) AS ge USING (order_id)
WHERE cco.pizza_id IN (1, 2)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Revenue per order (base price + extras)
SELECT order_id,
       base_price + extras_qty AS order_revenue
FROM (
     SELECT cco.order_id,
            CASE WHEN cco.pizza_id = 1 THEN 12 ELSE 10 END AS base_price,
            COALESCE(ge.total_extras, 0) AS extras_qty
     FROM pizza_clean_customer_orders AS cco
     JOIN pizza_clean_runner_orders  AS cro USING (order_id)
     LEFT JOIN (
          SELECT order_id, SUM(extras_count) AS total_extras
          FROM   pizza_get_extras
          GROUP BY order_id
     ) AS ge USING (order_id)
     WHERE cro.cancellation IS NULL
       AND cco.pizza_id IN (1, 2)
)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL: Total income earned from all delivered Meat Lovers and Vegetarian pizzas
SELECT SUM(base_price + extras_qty) AS total_income_usd
FROM (
     SELECT cco.order_id,
            CASE WHEN cco.pizza_id = 1 THEN 12  -- Meat Lovers
                 WHEN cco.pizza_id = 2 THEN 10  -- Vegetarian
            END AS base_price,
            COALESCE(ge.total_extras, 0) AS extras_qty
     FROM pizza_clean_customer_orders AS cco
     JOIN pizza_clean_runner_orders  AS cro USING (order_id)
     LEFT JOIN (
          SELECT order_id, SUM(extras_count) AS total_extras
          FROM   pizza_get_extras
          GROUP BY order_id
     ) AS ge USING (order_id)
     WHERE cro.cancellation IS NULL      -- filter out cancelled deliveries
       AND cco.pizza_id IN (1, 2)        -- only the two pizzas we price
);
```

Running the final query will return exactly one number (`total_income_usd`) — the full amount Pizza Runner earned from successfully delivered Meat Lovers and Vegetarian pizzas, with every extra topping charged at $1.
